course: dictionary
lesson: 240
title: Ally: a friend who helps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ally is a person, group or country that agrees to help and support you. Ally is a noun, so you can have one ally, or two or more allies.
explain: Ally can also be a verb, meaning to join with someone to help each other. Its verb forms are allies, allied and allying. «Cleopatra tried to keep Egypt free by allying with Roman leaders.» Here allying means joining with them for help.
explain: Use the context to check. «A friend who stands up for you is an ally.» Swap in a meaning: a friend who helps and supports you still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: An ally is a person, group or country that agrees to help and support you.
fact: «Allies» is the plural of ally: more than one ally.
fact: Countries form allies in wars, so they fight on the same side.
fact: By 1914 the big countries of Europe were tied together in two groups of allies, so one quarrel could pull in all the rest.
fact: Someone who supports a group that is treated unfairly can also be called an ally.
exercise: «Cleopatra tried to keep Egypt free by allying with Roman leaders.» What does allying mean here? | Leaving the country | Counting money | *Joining with someone to help and support each other | Fighting each other
exercise: Which word means a person who helps and supports you? | Enemy | Stranger | Rival | *Ally
exercise: «Real conquests needed local allies who hated their old rulers.» Which word is the plural of ally? | *allies | allying | ally | allied
test: Ayesha says «I will ally myself with Sam against the bullies.» What does ally yourself with mean? | To run away from | To copy | To ignore | *To join with someone to help and support them
test: Which sentence uses ally as a noun? | *Each country hoped for a strong ally in the war. | They are allying their teams today. | The children allied the boxes into a tower. | The two countries decided to ally against the enemy.
exam: In «tried to keep Egypt free by allying with Roman leaders», what part of speech is allying? | Adverb | Noun | Adjective | *Verb
